1
00:00:01,062 --> 00:00:05,253
Hello everyone, I'm Sérgio Fernandes, and
this is our project,

2
00:00:05,253 --> 00:00:06,943
IRIS Production Guardian.

3
00:00:06,943 --> 00:00:12,147
It is an application built entirely on top
of the InterSystems IRIS platform.

4
00:00:12,147 --> 00:00:14,310
It aims to solve a real problem:

5
00:00:14,310 --> 00:00:19,920
when an integration environment fails and
someone needs to understand what happened

6
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:21,475
as quickly as possible.

7
00:00:21,475 --> 00:00:26,882
You can't rely on a generic answer. Our
application is made up of three modules.

8
00:00:26,882 --> 00:00:28,572
The first is the Monitor,

9
00:00:28,646 --> 00:00:34,384
which is real-time monitoring of the state
of each Production.

10
00:00:34,384 --> 00:00:40,585
The second is the AI Incident
Investigator: when a component fails,

11
00:00:40,585 --> 00:00:42,899
we select that component,

12
00:00:42,899 --> 00:00:50,026
and within a time window it analyzes real
failure data and shows a structured

13
00:00:50,026 --> 00:00:51,272
investigation,

14
00:00:51,322 --> 00:00:56,412
so you can see the most likely hypothesis
for the cause

15
00:00:56,486 --> 00:01:03,383
and what cannot be stated with certainty.
But it never fixes anything on its own;

16
00:01:03,383 --> 00:01:09,514
it always depends on a human action. And
the third is the RAG Assistant.

17
00:01:09,514 --> 00:01:14,538
It answers questions about the project's
own documentation.

18
00:01:14,538 --> 00:01:18,795
So we can ask this Assistant any kind of
question,

19
00:01:18,795 --> 00:01:25,948
and it can only answer within the scope of
the project, nothing outside the project.

20
00:01:26,022 --> 00:01:33,099
We even created two versions of the query,
one with Gemini and one with Groq.

21
00:01:33,099 --> 00:01:35,948
Shall we go to the application?

22
00:01:39,014 --> 00:01:47,198
Hello everyone, so here we are looking at
our Production, where we have the Service,

23
00:01:47,198 --> 00:01:54,506
Process and Operations, with the rule that
if the message is high priority,

24
00:01:54,506 --> 00:02:01,034
it must land in this Priority Operation,
and if it is low priority,

25
00:02:01,034 --> 00:02:04,444
it lands in this File Output, okay?

26
00:02:04,518 --> 00:02:08,318
So this is the rule. We created a rule,

27
00:02:08,318 --> 00:02:14,748
and we can see that if the expression is
High, Critical or Medium,

28
00:02:14,748 --> 00:02:21,569
it goes to the Priority Output; otherwise,
it goes to the File Output.

29
00:02:21,569 --> 00:02:25,953
Here is our application, Production
Guardian.

30
00:02:25,953 --> 00:02:29,948
At this moment the Production is stopped,

31
00:02:30,022 --> 00:02:32,972
so we are going to start it here.

32
00:02:33,958 --> 00:02:35,372
And then...

33
00:02:36,614 --> 00:02:39,084
we can watch the Monitor here.

34
00:02:39,878 --> 00:02:43,936
Within a few seconds, it refreshes every
10 seconds,

35
00:02:43,936 --> 00:02:46,980
it will bring our Production up. There,

36
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:51,350
now we have a monitor of everything
happening right now.

37
00:02:51,350 --> 00:02:57,282
The idea is to create a loop that sends
messages and then watch the traffic,

38
00:02:57,282 --> 00:03:01,886
and that is when we start working with our
Guardian. First,

39
00:03:01,886 --> 00:03:07,271
I'll show that the output folders are
empty; nothing has arrived yet,

40
00:03:07,271 --> 00:03:08,988
nothing has been sent.

41
00:03:09,062 --> 00:03:16,058
So if we check this folder, which
corresponds to the File Output Operation,

42
00:03:16,058 --> 00:03:17,644
there is nothing.

43
00:03:20,070 --> 00:03:22,508
And the priority one is empty too.

44
00:03:23,750 --> 00:03:29,612
So we start with a loop of regular
messages

45
00:03:33,094 --> 00:03:34,764
from this moment on.

46
00:03:36,838 --> 00:03:42,892
We can search and confirm that the
messages are passing through the system,

47
00:03:42,892 --> 00:03:44,748
through the Production.

48
00:03:45,862 --> 00:03:51,436
If we check the regular output folder,
there are files there,

49
00:03:52,166 --> 00:03:54,220
and in the priority one, there are not.

50
00:03:56,102 --> 00:03:57,502
So...

51
00:03:58,214 --> 00:04:00,908
we can now send a

52
00:04:01,926 --> 00:04:04,844
high-priority message.

53
00:04:08,358 --> 00:04:10,444
We can also observe that

54
00:04:11,494 --> 00:04:16,858
it arrived in the high-priority one. So
our Monitor is working,

55
00:04:16,858 --> 00:04:22,136
it keeps counting the messages, it
refreshes every 10 seconds,

56
00:04:22,136 --> 00:04:27,755
and now comes our project: creating a real
unavailability problem,

57
00:04:27,755 --> 00:04:32,608
having the AI analyze it for us through
the Investigator,

58
00:04:32,608 --> 00:04:39,164
and then being able to interact with it in
these two models, Gemini and Groq,

59
00:04:39,238 --> 00:04:42,257
asking questions for it to answer.

60
00:04:42,257 --> 00:04:49,451
So the first thing I'm going to do is create a
block on the high-priority folder,

61
00:04:49,451 --> 00:04:52,204
so I'll change the permissions,

62
00:04:56,422 --> 00:04:58,092
changing them

63
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:01,420
to non-writable.

64
00:05:03,142 --> 00:05:07,116
I'll try to send another message

65
00:05:07,654 --> 00:05:09,054
to it.

66
00:05:11,238 --> 00:05:17,932
I'll just change the message name; it was
003, I'll switch it to 4.

67
00:05:20,870 --> 00:05:23,820
We'll see that as soon as it refreshes,

68
00:05:24,614 --> 00:05:28,629
the Process status will appear here as
degraded,

69
00:05:28,629 --> 00:05:32,812
and the Priority Output Operation as
degraded too.

70
00:05:37,254 --> 00:05:39,532
So that's where we are.

71
00:05:40,774 --> 00:05:42,174
However,

72
00:05:42,630 --> 00:05:51,004
we keep sending, in a loop, a message every 60
seconds to the File Output Operation.

73
00:05:51,004 --> 00:05:54,792
So when the next message goes through,

74
00:05:54,792 --> 00:06:00,973
that processing host is expected to return
to a healthy state,

75
00:06:00,973 --> 00:06:05,260
while the Guardian Priority stays
degraded.

76
00:06:06,086 --> 00:06:07,884
Here in the Investigator,

77
00:06:09,126 --> 00:06:11,084
if we look at it,

78
00:06:11,846 --> 00:06:17,501
we can run an analysis; I can have the AI
run an analysis for us.

79
00:06:17,501 --> 00:06:21,068
I'll ask here for the last three minutes.

80
00:06:27,718 --> 00:06:31,089
We improved the interface a little,

81
00:06:31,089 --> 00:06:38,409
so now we have this loader here while
waiting for the AI to respond with the

82
00:06:38,409 --> 00:06:39,809
analysis.

83
00:06:41,606 --> 00:06:46,642
It says here that there was an error, a
timeout failure,

84
00:06:46,642 --> 00:06:53,567
and here it gives a summary saying that it
is degraded and what is happening.

85
00:06:53,567 --> 00:07:00,492
All of this is what the AI did for us.
Here it says what the error was, 5005.

86
00:07:01,190 --> 00:07:07,595
It says here which incident it is, which
is this text file number 4.

87
00:07:07,595 --> 00:07:11,834
The observations are the items that
happened,

88
00:07:11,834 --> 00:07:15,884
what it managed to look up about the
error.

89
00:07:16,742 --> 00:07:20,503
It says what the hypotheses for the
problem are,

90
00:07:20,503 --> 00:07:25,595
so it always depends on a human action to
carry out the solution.

91
00:07:25,595 --> 00:07:31,001
It does the whole analysis and delivers
everything ready to be fixed,

92
00:07:31,001 --> 00:07:33,900
but it does not fix it automatically.

93
00:07:36,198 --> 00:07:42,796
And here it says what problems it faced in
building a more elaborate hypothesis.

94
00:07:42,796 --> 00:07:43,736
For example,

95
00:07:43,786 --> 00:07:50,137
there is no direct confirmation in the log
of why the operating system denied

96
00:07:50,137 --> 00:07:51,539
opening the file,

97
00:07:51,539 --> 00:07:56,735
whether it was lack of permission or
something like disk space.

98
00:07:56,735 --> 00:08:01,436
So when it can't determine something with
full certainty,

99
00:08:01,510 --> 00:08:05,799
it says so here in the gaps, which gap it
found.

100
00:08:05,799 --> 00:08:12,948
And it gives the next step on how to solve
the problem. So for the support team,

101
00:08:12,948 --> 00:08:18,220
for example, which is called in when there
is a production,

102
00:08:18,220 --> 00:08:25,458
integration or interoperability problem,
our project gives them a more assertive,

103
00:08:25,458 --> 00:08:31,356
faster answer, straight to the point,
about what needs to be done.

104
00:08:31,430 --> 00:08:36,492
There is documentation related to what it
consulted.

105
00:08:37,478 --> 00:08:45,804
Here in these RAG Assistants, we can ask,
for example, what this error is.

106
00:09:00,966 --> 00:09:07,758
And then it gives the meaning and the
step-by-step order of execution:

107
00:09:07,758 --> 00:09:15,326
check the directory, confirm the permission. It
always stays within our scope.

108
00:09:15,326 --> 00:09:22,700
It gives a summary of corrective actions,
all of this done by the AI for us.

109
00:09:23,622 --> 00:09:26,476
If I ask here, for example,

110
00:09:38,310 --> 00:09:46,188
it cannot answer because it is outside our
scope. Here we have the English version,

111
00:09:47,974 --> 00:09:49,374
okay,

112
00:09:49,702 --> 00:09:53,260
and we also have light mode and dark mode.

113
00:09:53,958 --> 00:09:58,156
So now let's restore it and try sending
again.

114
00:10:07,270 --> 00:10:11,532
Before restoring, take a look at our
messages.

115
00:10:12,550 --> 00:10:17,164
So we have the low-priority ones arriving
at the destination,

116
00:10:17,958 --> 00:10:20,204
and the high-priority one,

117
00:10:21,062 --> 00:10:30,508
with the indication there of that timeout
error, error 5005, okay?

118
00:10:33,030 --> 00:10:36,940
So what we need to do is follow

119
00:10:38,150 --> 00:10:43,982
what the Monitor did, what the
Investigator and the RAG suggested to us,

120
00:10:43,982 --> 00:10:46,412
so we are going to restore it.

121
00:10:47,270 --> 00:10:49,132
It will send again

122
00:10:49,702 --> 00:10:56,073
the message, and now we change the file
name to 5, leaving 4 with the error,

123
00:10:56,073 --> 00:11:00,684
because we'll resend it through the
application itself.

124
00:11:02,758 --> 00:11:04,556
So we send 5.

125
00:11:05,670 --> 00:11:12,003
And then it should refresh like this. It
has refreshed, and now the system is back.

126
00:11:12,003 --> 00:11:16,428
So this really validates what the
Investigator brought us,

127
00:11:23,558 --> 00:11:28,908
and also validates the tips from the RAG,
which we did here with two models,

128
00:11:28,908 --> 00:11:34,188
Gemini and Groq. I only showed Groq, but I
could have shown Gemini as well.

129
00:11:41,158 --> 00:11:47,089
It takes a while because it is processing
everything that happened in the last five

130
00:11:47,089 --> 00:11:48,876
minutes and bringing back

131
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:51,244
the results.

132
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:53,150
Okay?

133
00:11:56,838 --> 00:12:01,547
So we can go there; this is the rule, it
was created.

134
00:12:01,547 --> 00:12:08,210
It has the part of the message that it
checks for High, Critical or Medium,

135
00:12:08,210 --> 00:12:11,852
and then sends to the Priority Operation,

136
00:12:12,902 --> 00:12:19,744
or if it is none of those three severities, it
sends to the regular File Output,

137
00:12:19,744 --> 00:12:20,788
okay?

138
00:12:20,838 --> 00:12:27,504
And then we can look at our messages
again. This one, the one with the error,

139
00:12:27,504 --> 00:12:28,904
we can resend.

140
00:12:30,758 --> 00:12:32,716
Do a resend on it,

141
00:12:35,270 --> 00:12:41,388
resend, and now we view the message,

142
00:12:42,662 --> 00:12:45,004
this one, which is the one with the error.

143
00:12:46,694 --> 00:12:53,590
We can see that now it managed to reach the
destination and came back successfully.

144
00:12:53,590 --> 00:12:55,916
Our project also includes...

145
00:12:58,534 --> 00:13:03,853
the prompts. So we have a Git commit with
all the prompts we used,

146
00:13:03,853 --> 00:13:08,849
everything we did in the project, so that
it can be consulted;

147
00:13:08,849 --> 00:13:15,135
it will be included in the description.
Okay? That concludes our presentation.

148
00:13:15,135 --> 00:13:17,472
Thank you, see you next time!
